{"term":"scar","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6715c973bd346aec9d","definition":"A permanent mark on the skin, sometimes caused by the healing of a wound.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["cicatrice","cicatrix"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["fire scar","labelscar","leaf scar","Red Scar","scarface","scarless","scarlike","scar limestone","scarproof","scarry","scar tissue","scar tree","top scar","trial of scar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:270de23226b833b165","definition":"A permanent negative effect on someone's mind, caused by a traumatic experience.","example":"Thus, it is wise to avoid cultivating an emotional scar, as it can play havoc with your happiness and success.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["cicatrice","cicatrix"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["fire scar","labelscar","leaf scar","Red Scar","scarface","scarless","scarlike","scar limestone","scarproof","scarry","scar tissue","scar tree","top scar","trial of scar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bed4c54868f9220206","definition":"Any permanent mark resulting from damage.","example":"Her age-old weapons, flood and fire, left scars on the canyon which time will never efface.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["cicatrice","cicatrix"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["fire scar","labelscar","leaf scar","Red Scar","scarface","scarless","scarlike","scar limestone","scarproof","scarry","scar tissue","scar tree","top scar","trial of scar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scar#Engli